## Trust

Tool plugins execute trusted Python code in the datalab API process.
{% if tool_ui_kind == "in-app" %}
This plugin also loads trusted JavaScript in the signed-in datalab application.
{% endif %}
Deployment administrators must review source code, dependencies, compiled
assets, maintainers, and release provenance before installation or upgrade.

## Availability and route access

Override `ToolProvider.is_available(context)` when access depends on the
current user. The result controls catalog visibility, launch permission, and
all browser-authenticated routes in the provider blueprint. An exception denies
access, so availability checks should be small and reliable.

`is_available(context)` is not called for service-authenticated provider
routes. Providers using `ToolRouteAuth.SERVICE` must authorize clients in
`authenticate_service_request()` and in their handler logic.
